{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.keys",
    "description": "Template library: the two RELATIONAL shapes of docs/nonroad-logging-county.md \u00a74.5 and \u00a74.6, reduced to the arithmetic half that a template can carry. Both are most-specific-match lookups, and neither is an equi-join by itself. The convention (docs/esm-conventions.md \u00a73) is to precompute an EFFECTIVE KEY column with these templates and then join on it with a plain `join.on`, so the run-time relational step stays a single equi-join and the precedence logic stays in one place. `presence` arguments are booleans a caller computes with a `max`-semiring aggregate over the target relation. Layered on moves.identifiers: both ladder templates invoke `scc_zero_tail` by reference (esm-spec \u00a79.7.3 registration-time body checking), so the truncation arithmetic exists once in the repository. Three later templates are not lookups at all: `flat_relation_major` / `flat_relation_minor` decode a FLAT row relation whose key is a product of two axes -- position `p` of a relation laid out in blocks of `block_size` is member `major` of the outer axis and `minor` of the inner one. That layout is finding F14's workaround made concrete: the port's output key sets are ragged, a `ragged` index set does not evaluate (F14), and a rectangular axis emits keys the snapshot does not have, so every such product is carried as a flat relation with the two coordinates as ordinary key COLUMNS. Both delegate the one floor division to `flat_relation_block_index`, so `minor` is defined as `position - block_size x major` in the only place `major` is computed and the two can never disagree about a boundary.\n\n`model_year_in_range` is the fourth shape and the most repeated one in the repository: MOVES keys a great many of its lookup tables by an INCLUSIVE model-year band -- `temperatureadjustment`, `evefficiency`, `fleetavgadjustment`, `pm10emissionratio`, `emissionratebyage` -- and the band is always the residual predicate left over after the equi-join keys, so it is a `filter` and not a `join.on` (docs/esm-conventions.md 3). Before this template the two-clause `and` was written out thirty-four times across four fixtures, once per lookup, with the inclusivity of each end decided thirty-four times. Twenty-six were replaced when the template was introduced; `fixtures/process-refueling.esm` contributed the other eight -- three on `fleetavgadjustment` and five on `temperatureadjustment` -- and had them only because it was authored on a branch that started before this template existed. That is the ordinary cost of two slices in parallel, and the reason to look for it on merge rather than to trust that the newest document uses the newest library. The column names differ between tables -- `minModelYearID`/`maxModelYearID` on some and `beginModelYearID`/`endModelYearID` on others -- which is exactly why the shape, and not the columns, is what a template can carry.\n\n`model_year_in_range` is now one line: it delegates to `in_inclusive_range`, the same shape under the name it always had. MOVES bands ages exactly as it bands model years and `generalfuelratio` carries BOTH bands on one row (`fixtures/process-crankcase-running.esm`), so the choice was to write the two comparisons out a thirty-fifth time under a different column name or to admit that the model-year name was never the shape. The caller-facing template keeps its name and its parameter names, because they read correctly at every one of its existing call sites.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "nonroad",
      "joins",
      "template-library"
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "./identifiers.esm",
      "only": [
        "scc_zero_tail"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "scc_equipment_chain_key": {
      "params": [
        "scc",
        "has_exact",
        "has_zero3"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          "has_exact",
          "scc",
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              "has_zero3",
              {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "scc_zero_tail",
                "bindings": {
                  "scc": "scc",
                  "tail_scale": 1000
                }
              },
              {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "scc_zero_tail",
                "bindings": {
                  "scc": "scc",
                  "tail_scale": 1000000
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "scc_lookup_ladder_key": {
      "params": [
        "scc",
        "has_exact",
        "has_zero2",
        "has_zero4"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          "has_exact",
          "scc",
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              "has_zero2",
              {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "scc_zero_tail",
                "bindings": {
                  "scc": "scc",
                  "tail_scale": 100
                }
              },
              {
                "op": "ifelse",
                "args": [
                  "has_zero4",
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "scc_zero_tail",
                    "bindings": {
                      "scc": "scc",
                      "tail_scale": 10000
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "scc_zero_tail",
                    "bindings": {
                      "scc": "scc",
                      "tail_scale": 1000000
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "latest_at_or_before_key": {
      "params": [
        "has_at_or_before",
        "latest_at_or_before",
        "earliest_after"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          "has_at_or_before",
          "latest_at_or_before",
          "earliest_after"
        ]
      }
    },
    "in_inclusive_range": {
      "params": [
        "value",
        "first",
        "last"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "and",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "<=",
            "args": [
              "first",
              "value"
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "<=",
            "args": [
              "value",
              "last"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "model_year_in_range": {
      "params": [
        "model_year",
        "first_model_year",
        "last_model_year"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "in_inclusive_range",
        "bindings": {
          "value": "model_year",
          "first": "first_model_year",
          "last": "last_model_year"
        }
      }
    },
    "state_default_precedence": {
      "params": [
        "has_state_row",
        "state_id",
        "default_state_id"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          "has_state_row",
          "state_id",
          "default_state_id"
        ]
      }
    },
    "flat_relation_major": {
      "params": [
        "position",
        "block_size"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "flat_relation_block_index",
            "bindings": {
              "position": "position",
              "block_size": "block_size"
            }
          },
          1
        ]
      }
    },
    "flat_relation_minor": {
      "params": [
        "position",
        "block_size"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "position",
                  1
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "block_size",
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "flat_relation_block_index",
                    "bindings": {
                      "position": "position",
                      "block_size": "block_size"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          1
        ]
      }
    },
    "flat_relation_block_index": {
      "params": [
        "position",
        "block_size"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "floor",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "position",
                  1
                ]
              },
              "block_size"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
